Every point he makes is a point that makes him like Angband less.  The
only level 65+ monsters in nethack are a couple of the demon
lords/princes.  In angband, there are scores of them.  In angband, you
max out at level 50, not 30, and it is quite possible to get to level
50 with minimal help from potions of experience.  I've never gotten
past level 16 in nethack without !oGL, wraith corpses or *cubus
dancing.

In angband, the only real difference between a mage with max str and a
warrior with max str is the maximum number of attacks per round.  As
you note, in nethack, 18 INT Bar and 25 STR Wiz are quite different
beasts from 18 INT Wiz and 25 Str Bar.  However, in angband, warriors
can never cast spells, unlike nethack, where any character of high
enough INT/XL can learn spells and cast with a modicum of efficiency. 
The biggest problem with angband (in the 2.8.x days) is that mages had
very few high level spells that allowed them to actually play like
mages.  In nethack, (3.2+ anyway), Wiz can do a better job of playing
their role all the way through the game.

